# How to cite ED-MORE (https://citation-file-format.github.io). Each release pull request sets the
# version and the release date; contributors add themselves to the authors in their first pull request.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use ED-MORE, please cite it as below, with the version you used.
title: "ED-MORE: Ecosystem Demography — Modular, Open, Reproducible, Extensible"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Xiangtao
    affiliation: Cornell University
repository-code: https://github.com/EDmodel/ED-MORE
# The concept DOI: it stands for every version and resolves to the latest. Zenodo gives each release
# its own DOI as well (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23674060 lists them).
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23674060
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.1
date-released: 2026-10-26
abstract: >
  ED-MORE is a size- and age-structured terrestrial biosphere model, advanced on a fast (sub-daily)
  and a slow (daily and longer) timescale, whose science follows the Ecosystem Demography model.
keywords:
  - terrestrial biosphere model
  - vegetation demography
  - Ecosystem Demography
  - Fortran
